            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41992-gzip",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41992 medium vulnerability for gzip package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU gzip contains a global buffer overflow vulnerability in the LZH decompression logic caused by improper reuse of shared global state between different decompression formats within a single execution. GNU gzip maintains a global array that is shared across the LZ77, LZW, and LZH decompression routines and is not reinitialized between files processed in the same invocation.\nBy decompressing a specially crafted LZW file followed by a specially crafted LZH file in a single gzip -d command, an attacker can poison the shared global state and subsequently trigger an out‑of‑bounds read in the LZH decoder. The LZH decompression logic follows stale values left in the shared array, causing reads past the end of the allocated global buffer.\n\nThis issue has been fixed in the commit 63dbf6b3b9e6e781df1a6a64e609b10e23969681"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-41992",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41992\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: gzip\nVersion: 1.10-4ubuntu4.1\nFix Version: 1.10-4ubuntu4.2\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-41992](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-41992)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41992**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | gzip  | 1.10-4ubuntu4.1  | 1.10-4ubuntu4.2  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04  | [CVE-2026-41992](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-41992)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/gzip@1.10-4ubuntu4.1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-22.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-48962-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-48962 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "IO::Compress versions before 2.220 for Perl can execute arbitrary code in File::GlobMapper via an attacker-controlled output glob.\n\n_parseOutputGlob() wraps the caller-supplied output glob string in double quotes and stores it in the parser state; _getFiles() then runs the stored expression through eval STRING. A literal double quote in the output glob closes the dquote wrapper, and the characters that follow are evaluated as Perl.\n\nArbitrary Perl in the output glob executes at the calling process's privilege."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48962",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-48962\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.7\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-48962](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48962)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-48962**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.7  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04  | [CVE-2026-48962](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48962)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.34.0-3ubuntu1.7?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-22.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-10041-libpam-modules",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-10041 medium vulnerability for libpam-modules package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was found in PAM. The secret information is stored in memory, where the attacker can trigger the victim program to execute by sending characters to its standard input (stdin). As this occurs, the attacker can train the branch predictor to execute an ROP chain speculatively. This flaw could result in leaked passwords, such as those found in /etc/shadow while performing authentications."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2024-10041",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-10041\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpam-modules\nVersion: 1.4.0-11ubuntu2.6\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2024-10041](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2024-10041)",
