            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-27587-libssl3",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-27587 low vulnerability for libssl3 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OpenSSL 3.0.0 through 3.3.2 on the PowerPC architecture is vulnerable to a Minerva attack, exploitable by measuring the time of signing of random messages using the EVP_DigestSign API, and then using the private key to extract the K value (nonce) from the signatures. Next, based on the bit size of the extracted nonce, one can compare the signing time of full-sized nonces to signatures that used smaller nonces, via statistical tests. There is a side-channel in the P-364 curve that allows private key extraction (also, there is a dependency between the bit size of K and the size of the side channel). NOTE: This CVE is disputed because the OpenSSL security policy explicitly notes that any side channels which require same physical system to be detected are outside of the threat model for the software. The timing signal is so small that it is infeasible to be detected without having the attacking process running on the same physical system."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2025-27587",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-27587\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libssl3\nVersion: 3.0.2-0ubuntu1.25\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2025-27587](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2025-27587)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-27587**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libssl3  | 3.0.2-0ubuntu1.25  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04  | [CVE-2025-27587](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2025-27587)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libssl3@3.0.2-0ubuntu1.25?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-22.04\u0026upstream=openssl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8932-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8932 low vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libcurl would reuse a previously created connection even when some mTLS config\nrelated option had been changed that should have prohibited reuse.\n\nlibcurl keeps previously used connections in a connection pool for subsequent\ntransfers to reuse if one of them matches the setup. However, some TLS\nsettings related to client certificates were left out from the configuration\nmatch checks, making them match too easily. In particular options related to\nthe private key."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-8932",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8932\nSeverity: low\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 7.81.0-1ubuntu1.25\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-8932](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-8932)",
